<title>USA: Western Resources Q3 hurt by weather.</title>
<headline>Western Resources Q3 hurt by weather.</headline>
<dateline>TOPEKA, Kan. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Resources Inc said Friday unseasonably cool weather in July and August cut $0.26 a share off third quarter earnings.</p>
<p>Cooling degree days, a measure of air conditioning demand, were 23 percent off last year's third quarter totals and 17 percent lower than normal, the utility company said.</p>
<p>Wholesale electricty, however, rose 42 pecent in the quarter, the company said.</p>
<p>Earlier Friday, the company reported earnings of $0.87 a share for the third quarter, down from $1.10 a year ago.</p>
<p>Shares rose 1/8 to 29-3/4 Friday.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
